    {
      "id": "bcd47e41-5580-4d5d-9f2f-e29e78dd0238",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -560,
        -480
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 832,
        "content": "## track homeowners association architectural review requests with AI\n\n### How it works\n\nEvery home improvement that touches the outside of the house starts with an architectural review request. Small HOAs run this on email and paper, and owners regularly say they never heard back, while boards miss their own deadlines and the request auto-expires.\n\n1. An owner submits the change on a hosted form. The request is checked, and a missing email, address or modification type is logged and flagged to the board.\n2. An AI assistant reviews the request against typical community rules and returns advisory flags, a two sentence summary for the board, and a warm acknowledgment paragraph for the owner.\n3. The request is stored in the ARC Requests sheet with a 30 day review deadline. The owner gets an acknowledgment email with that deadline, and the board gets an email alert.\n4. When the board decides, a webhook records approved, approved with conditions, or denied, updates the row, and emails the owner a decision letter.\n5. Every morning a sweep finds requests inside the 5 day window and reminds the board by email, so no request is forgotten until it auto-expires.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Add the workflows Google credential to the HOA spreadsheet (tabs ARC Requests and Errors).\n- Connect Gmail for the acknowledgment, decision letter, board alerts and deadline reminders.\n- Set the board inbox address on the three board email nodes.\n- Share the form link with owners. Paste the form URL into the ARC Request Form trigger.\n\n### Customization\n\n- Change the 30 day review deadline in Normalize ARC Request.\n- Change the 5 day sweep window in Find Near Deadline.\n- Swap the board email for Slack, Telegram or SMS if your board lives somewhere else."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
